    "title": "PureWow Picks: Lindsay Lohan Is on a Quest to Find Better Nonstick Pans - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Philip Mutz ,\n8 hours ago\nPureWow editors select every item that appears on this page, and some items may be gifted to us. Additionally, PureWow may earn compensation through affiliate links within the story. All prices are accurate upon date of publish. You can learn more about the affiliate process here .\nA household name, especially for any millennial? Britney, Paris and, of course, Lindsay.\nI sat down for an exclusive interview with Mean Girls star and iconic millennial Lindsay Lohan, where she revealed her six PureWow Picks—items she can't live without—for parenting, spending a long day on her feet or for monitoring her sleep.\nHere, six of Lindsay’s absolute faves.\n1. Nanit Camera Babylist\n“[I love] my Nanit camera that I use for my son, because I'm working a lot, so even when he's napping, I can still watch him and see him, and feel like I'm there, and even talk to him through it.”\nBuy It $250 ; $150 2. Alaia Patent Ballet Flats Alaia\n“Because I live in them. [They’re] the easiest for going out, taking my son to the park, even going to dinner. There’s black dressier ones and patent ones, and they're just so comfortable. I’ve worn them forever.”\nBuy It $1,250 3. Nonstick Pans Hexclad\n“I'm always on the hunt for new, good non-stick pans and cookware. Because [sometimes] it doesn't work. Even today, I used one that I thought was gonna be great, and then the eggs were sticking!”\nBuy It $399 ; $329 4. Oura Ring Babylist\n“It’s just something that I use daily. I check every morning to track my sleep, mainly.”\nBuy It from $399 5. Levi’s x RE/DONE Jeans and RE/DONE White T-Shirt RE/DONE\n“My go-to uniform is always good jeans and a white tee.”\nBuy the Jeans $395 Buy the shirt $125 6. Insight Timer App InsightTimer\n“An app on my phone that I use every day, aside from WhatsApp? I'd say Insight Timer. You can do meditation, or just some breath work.”\nGet for free\n3",
    "summary": "Additionally, PureWow may earn compensation through affiliate links within the story. I sat down for an exclusive interview with Mean Girls star and iconic millennial Lindsay Lohan, where she revealed her six PureWow Picks—items she can't live without—for parenting, spending a long day on her feet or for monitoring her sleep. “[I love] my Nanit camera that I use for my son, because I'm working a lot, so even when he's napping, I can still watch him and see him, and feel like I'm there, and even talk to him through it.”",
